NAME
    cp - copy files and directories

SYNOPSIS
    cp [-r | -rf] <src> <dst>

DESCRIPTION
    Copies <src> to <dst> inside the shell sandbox. If <dst> is an
    existing directory, <src> is copied into it under its base name. An
    existing destination file is overwritten without prompting. Copying
    a file onto itself is refused.

    Copying a directory requires -r (or -rf).

OPTIONS
    -r, -rf
        Copy directories recursively (flags matched case-insensitively).

EXAMPLES
    cp /Logs/notes.txt /Logs/notes.bak.txt
    cp -r /Logs/Run1 /Logs/Run1Backup

EXIT STATUS
    0   Copy succeeded.
    1   Missing arguments, path outside sandbox, source missing,
        directory copied without -r, or I/O error.

SEE ALSO
    mv(1), rm(1), ls(1), touch(1)
